From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaq Question <zaquestion@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] place new floating clients over the focused client

dwl gives a newly mapped client whatever geometry the client itself
reports, and a fresh xdg toplevel reports x=y=0. For tiled clients that
does not matter -- the layout overwrites it immediately -- but a floating
one keeps it, so every float appears in the monitor's top-left corner
regardless of what was on screen or where the pointer was.

Place it over the client that was focused at map time instead, copying
that client's size along with its position. That makes a float read as
something that opened "on top of what I was doing" rather than as a window
that jumped to the corner. The immediate consumer is ~/scripts/footpager,
the scrollback-in-nvim pager bound to ctrl+shift+[ in foot.ini: the pager
lands exactly over the terminal whose buffer it is showing.

The new client is already in fstack by this point (mapnotify inserts it
before applying rules), so the walk skips itself and takes the next
visible client on the same monitor. With nothing else on screen the loop
finds no candidate and the corner placement stands.
---
 dwl.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dwl.c b/dwl.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/dwl.c
+++ b/dwl.c
@@ -1977,7 +1977,7 @@
 {
 	/* Called when the surface is mapped, or ready to display on-screen. */
 	Client *p = NULL;
-	Client *w, *c = wl_container_of(listener, c, map);
+	Client *f, *w, *c = wl_container_of(listener, c, map);
 	Monitor *m;
 	int i;

@@ -2028,6 +2028,20 @@
 	} else {
 		applyrules(c);
 	}
+
+	/* Drop a new floating client onto whichever client was focused when it
+	 * appeared, taking that client's size as well as its position. Without
+	 * this it lands in the monitor's top-left corner: dwl resizes it to its
+	 * own geometry, and a freshly mapped xdg toplevel reports x=y=0.
+	 * c is already in fstack by this point, hence testing f != c. */
+	if (c->isfloating) {
+		wl_list_for_each(f, &fstack, flink) {
+			if (f != c && VISIBLEON(f, c->mon)) {
+				resize(c, f->geom, 0);
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	printstatus();

 unset_fullscreen:
